    <!-- M8.5 spec §2: the opt-in per-tag breakdown, beneath the tiles above. Nothing
         under this header renders at all while the developer setting is off — see
         BreakdownSection's own KDoc for the three states an empty row list can mean. -->
    <string name="home_breakdown_header">By server</string>
    <!-- %1$s and %2$s are already-formatted byte counts (formatByteCount), same as the
         DOWN/UP tiles above — never raw numbers (M8.5 spec §10.1). -->
    <string name="home_breakdown_row_traffic">%1$s ↓ · %2$s ↑</string>
    <!-- Shown in place of rows when the setting is on, the active server is a
         pasted (RAW_JSON) config, and no rows have arrived this connection.
         Deliberately names NO reason (ruling R51, finding N4): Home cannot see which
         branch the session ran. The pure passthrough branch (ARCHITECTURE.md §6) cannot
         carry a stats block, but an override-branch session whose breakdown was dropped
         by the Metrics tag-collision degrade looks identical from here, and the old
         "config runs unmodified" reason was false for it. The honest specific reason
         needs a per-session signal from the service, deferred to Part 3 (R43). "right
         now" (review M-C): a WORKING override-branch session also shows this until its
         first metrics poll returns rows, so a claim about the whole connection would be
         briefly false there; "right now" is true in every case. The resource name
         reflects when it is shown, not what it claims. -->
    <string name="home_breakdown_unavailable_passthrough">Per-server traffic isn\'t available for this connection right now</string>

